{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Design and Colors"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about colors."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the graphic layout of an IT solution, functional requirements of a business through the IT solution, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "monotony"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a routine that never changes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I used to create designs only with cool colors but I realized that even if they are relaxing, they can lead to monotony and therefore lack of impact."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cool colors"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "those that generate a relaxed atmosphere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Cool colors are green, blue and purple; they are relaxing and calming colors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "warm colors"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "those that generate a passionate atmosphere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Yeah, warm colors are red, orange and yellow; they're passionate and energizing colors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lack "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something missing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I used to create designs only with cool colors but I realized that even if they are relaxing, they can lead to monotony and therefore lack of impact."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "atmosphere"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "synonym of environment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, I want to have a happy atmosphere for the design. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "freshness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that is cool"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I used to put some orange to give vitality and green to give freshness to the design; users would find it friendlier. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You can use <strong>used to</strong> and <strong>would</strong> to describe situations that happened frequently in the past.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When I started creating designs, I used to create designs only with cool colors but I realized that even if they are relaxing, they can lead to monotony and therefore lack of impact. So, in my latest designs I would combine the two types of colors in order not to become predictab"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to put some orange to give vitality and green to give freshness to the design; users would find it friendlier."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <p>Both <strong>used to</strong> and <strong>would</strong> are used for talking about past habits or routines.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>I <strong>used to work</strong> as a software designer at that company, but I quit last year.</i></p> <p><i>Every time I could, I <strong>would grab</strong> some coloring pencils and paper. I loved drawing. </i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>However, there are some aspects you need to consider when talking about situations in the past with <strong>used to</strong> and <strong>would</strong>:</p> <ol> <li>When you use <strong>would</strong>, you have to mention the period of time in which the situations happened, while this is not necessary with <strong>used to</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><strong><i>When I was little</i></strong><i>, I <strong>would mix</strong> all kind of colors in my drawings.</i></p> <p><i>I <strong>used to</strong> mix all kind of colors in my drawings. </i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ol start=\"2\"> <li>Another difference between <strong>used to</strong> and <strong>would</strong> is that you cannot use stative verbs such as <i>feel, love</i>, or <i>be</i> with <strong>would</strong>, but it is possible to do it with <strong>used to</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>When I was a college student, I <strong>used to love</strong> painting.</i></p> <p><i>When I was a college student, I <strong>would paint</strong> a lot. </i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>This is the structure you use to make sentences with used to or would:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + <strong>used to/ would</strong>+ verb infinitive + complement.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Warm and Cool Colors"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Colors are divided into two categories <span class=\"strong\">warm</span> and <span class=\"strong\">cool</span> colors."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might want to use some red, in that way you can give accent to the design, it can give energy to the web page. I used to put some orange to give vitality and green to give freshness to the design; users would find it friendlier."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Warm colors are red, orange and yellow; they're passionate and energizing colors. Cool colors are green, blue and purple; they are relaxing and calming colors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Colors play an important role when designing web pages or similar. Colors are really subjective since they produce different feelings on people. Sometimes, depending on the culture or personal preferences, colors can evoke happiness or sadness.&nbsp;</p>  <p><strong>Warm colors</strong> are red, orange, yellow and all of their variations. These colors can produce a sense of happiness, energy or passion. These are primary colors and are not made by mixing a cool and a warm color.</p> <p><strong>Cool colors</strong> are blue, green and purple. These colors can produce a sense of relaxed or calmed atmosphere. Blue is also a primary color, and by combining it with some of those primary colors, we can obtain other colors as green or purple.</p>  <p>When you create a design, make sure you choose the colors carefully depending on the impression you want to create on users.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read about how to use warm and cool colors in web designs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a poster, write the most important advices. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give an oral presentation to your partners to explain how to use colors in the system design properly. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about how to use warm and cool colors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write the most important advices on how to use cool and warm colors."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners the most important advices on how to use cool and warm colors.  "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Hi Victor, I really appreciate your help checking the design I have for the web page.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: No problem Kelly, you know you can count on me. Let's check that design.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Look, here I have the design I came up with.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: Nice! You really did a good job with the font, shapes, and balance of information, but you'd better change colors.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Why? I think that those colors are appropriate for the web page.<br /><br />"}, {"time": "21700", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: Well, the combination you have is not appropriate, so you might want to check how to use and combine colors. You only used cool colors, there aren't any warm colors.<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Warm and cool colors?<br /><span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: Yeah, warm colors are red, orange and yellow; they're passionate and energizing colors. Cool colors are green, blue and purple; they are relaxing, calming colors.<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Why isn't a good idea to have only cool colors?<br /><span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: When I started creating designs, I used to create designs only with cool colors but I realized that even if they are relaxing, they can lead to monotony and therefore lack of impact. So, in my latest designs, I would combine the two types of colors in order not to become predictable.<br /><br />"}, {"time": "63600", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: How can I have a nice combination of both?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: You might want to use some red, in that way you can give accent to the design, it can give energy to the web page. I used to put some orange to give vitality and green to give freshness to the design; users would find it friendlier.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Kelly</span>: Well, I want to have a happy atmosphere for the design. What color may I use?<br /><span class=\"strong\">Victor</span>: In that case, you ought to use a yellow color, in that way you are indicating a sense of happiness."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le03ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about previous experiences with design and colors."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give advice about how to integrate warm and cool colors in the system design."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How can we classify colors?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Colors can symbolize different things to various cultures, what meanings do colors have in your culture? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": 